# Architecture

Brane is an Electron desktop chat app that runs local GGUF models on-device via
`node-llama-cpp`. There is no backend or network; everything happens across three
Electron processes plus a shared layer.

## Process layers

- `src/main/**` — Node/Electron main process. Owns the window, the model runtime
  (`main/llama`), model discovery (`main/model`), persistence (`main/store`),
  logging (`main/logger`), and all `ipcMain` handlers.
- `src/preload/**` — the context-isolated bridge. Exposes a single typed
  `electronApi` object on `window` via `contextBridge`; declares its shape in
  `preload/api.d.ts` (global `ElectronApi`).
- `src/renderer/**` — the React 19 UI. Talks to the main process only through
  `window.electronApi`; it never imports from `main` or uses `ipcRenderer`.
- `src/shared/**` — types and constants shared across processes (notably
  `IpcChannels` and all IPC payload types). The single safe cross-layer import.

## Import boundaries

- Renderer code must not import from `src/main`. Cross-process contracts live in
  `@shared/types`.
- Use path aliases, never long relative chains: `@shared/types`, `@shared/*`,
  `@/*` (renderer root), `@test/*`.

## Commands

- `npm start` — run the app (electron-forge + Vite).
- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — Vitest.
- `npm run lint` / `npm run lint:fix` — ESLint (type-checked).
- `npm run format` — Prettier.
- `npm run typecheck` — project-wide `tsc -b`. Each layer has its own tsconfig
  (`typecheck:main|preload|renderer|test`).
